 p=BASE/'flows'/(slug+'.md');s=(ROOT/p).read_text('utf-8');s=s.replace('Source diagrams pending reconstruction and visual review.','Source figures have explicit review evidence; contextual/version limitations remain.')
 start=s.index('## Diagrams and review');end=s.index('The MUG is Version 3.0',start)
 body='## Diagrams and review\n\n'+''.join('- '+link(p,DOC/'pdf-figures'/('fig-%04d.md'%n),'Diagram fig-%04d'%n)+'.\n' for n in flowfigs.get(slug,[]))+''.join('- '+link(p,DOC/'tables'/('tbl-%04d.md'%n),'Complete table tbl-%04d'%n)+'.\n' for n in tn)+'\n'+link(p,DOC/'visual-coverage.md','Full MUG visual-coverage and limitations')+'. Source diagrams have Mermaid 12.3.0 rendering and visual-comparison records. Scenarios with no separate source graph use their complete usage table and narrative.\n\n'
 s=s[:start]+body+s[end:]
 if slug=='copy':s+='\n## Source direction evidence\n\nThe diagram shows original A→B and copy A→C. The usage table nevertheless prints From=A, To=B. Those claims are retained separately, not collapsed into one receiver. Issue-000003 remains open. '+cite(p,'§2.7 p16')+'\n'
 if slug=='duplicate-of-copy':s+='\n## Source direction and code evidence\n\nThe diagram shows original A→B, prior copy A→C, then Message 3 (DUPL) A→C. The table prints To=B and CopyDuplicate=CODU. The general CODU usage and the drawn DUPL label are both retained; issue-000003 remains open. '+cite(p,'§2.9 p18')+'\n'
